A||N||6||Elenor84||Drive belt replaced now new problem....||||1||
Z||000000||Elenor84||12-29-2001||02:16 AM||||Hey guys...probably the worst week of my fiero's life...first...burst side hose...then lower rad hose burst...replaced both...then my drivebelt snaped so today I replaced that...but when I fire her up she still over heates...and there is no hot air coming out of vents when I turn it on...so its obvestly a circulation problem..is it my water pump?  One other thing is that when I opened my radiator cap it was frozen pritty good...and I stuck my finger as far down as I could and it was all frozen...now could it be that my thermestate is busted or my rad cap?  Thx guys...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-29-2001||06:49 AM||||You have a frozen engine, not enough anti freeze. It wont circulate as ice. Your going to have to get the car inside a garage for a day or two to thaw it out, aint gonna happen outside. When it does thaw, drain it and add new coolant, 1/2 water, 1/2 anti freeze. Then run it and hope that the block or head hasnt cracked. Your only hope is that being a cast iron block and heads are harder to break than aluminum. If its got water in the oil after you run it a while, start hunting for a new engine. Best of luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||12-29-2001||12:31 PM||||Also make sure you always add coolant from the thermostat housing cap. If you are adding from the front rad. cap it is too low and the engine would have no coolant in it.<P>Check Ogre's article on coolant fill <A HREF="http://home.sprynet.com/~theogre/tunnel6/coolfill.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.sprynet.com/~theogre/tunnel6/coolfill.htm</A>   <P>He also has some good stuff on heat management his cave's main enterence is here <A HREF="http://home.sprynet.com/~theogre/tunnel6/" TARGET=_blank>http://home.sprynet.com/~theogre/tunnel6/</A> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Elenor84||12-29-2001||04:37 PM||||Alright, thx very much guys...just curious if I pluged in my block heater if that would do the same trick?  And were on the engine is the drain hole that hanes talkes about...I could not find it...thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||avengador1||12-29-2001||05:41 PM||||The drain holes are on the pipes under the sides of the car, they come out with a hex wrench. Make sure you soak them with penetrating oil first to help release them.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Elenor84||12-29-2001||06:16 PM||||I knew about the drain holes on each side...but hanes says that there is a hole in the radiator...both side pipes and then on the engine block...is this true?  And once again should I plug in my heater core and see if that will melt it...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||12-30-2001||12:57 AM||||You have to put it indoors to thaw it unless its warm enough outside for a few days and nites. running it frozen is asking for more overheating and head/block damage, and prob twist the water pump impeller off too. the radiator drain is on the bottom of the radiator. And it wont drain until it thaws out either. When it does thaw, check that none of the block freeze plugs have popped too, causing leaks.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 12-30-2001).]||||reg||1
